\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Iota Rulebook: Definitive First-Order Principles for Implementation
\f1\b0 \
These principles are extracted directly from the rulebook with no additions, interpretations, or omissions. They are structured for direct translation into code (data models, validation functions, game loop, scoring engine). Every rule is atomic, unambiguous, and self-contained. Use these as the sole source of truth for the app.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 1. Deck & Card Representation\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Total deck: 66 cards.\
\pard\tx940\tx1440\pardeftab720\li1440\fi-1440\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl1\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 64 unique regular cards: every combination of 4 colors \'d7 4 shapes \'d7 4 numbers.\
\pard\tx1660\tx2160\pardeftab720\li2160\fi-2160\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl2\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u9642 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Colors: \{blue, red, yellow, green\}\
\ls1\ilvl2\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u9642 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Shapes: \{triangle, plus, square, circle\}\
\ls1\ilvl2\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u9642 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Numbers: \{1, 2, 3, 4\}\
\ls1\ilvl2\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u9642 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Face value of a regular card = its number.\
\pard\tx940\tx1440\pardeftab720\li1440\fi-1440\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl1\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 2 identical Wild cards.\
\pard\tx1660\tx2160\pardeftab720\li2160\fi-2160\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl2\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u9642 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Face value of any Wild = 0.\
\ls1\ilvl2\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u9642 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 A Wild has no inherent properties until assigned (see \'a75).\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Cards are distinct objects. Regular cards are immutable tuples (color, shape, number). Wilds are a special type WILD.\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Deck is shuffled once at start. Draw pile is a stack (top = next card drawn). Discarded/traded cards go to the 
\f0\b bottom
\f1\b0  of the draw pile (in the order chosen by the player).\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 2. Grid & Position Representation\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0
\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The playing area is an infinite integer grid (x: int, y: int).\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Each cell can hold at most one card (regular or Wild).\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Starter card is placed at any chosen origin (e.g., (0,0)); all other placements are relative to existing cards.\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Orthogonal adjacency only (no diagonals). A card at (x,y) is adjacent to (x\'b11,y) or (x,y\'b11).\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 A 
\f0\b contiguous segment
\f1\b0  in a row (fixed y, varying x) or column (fixed x, varying y) is a maximal sequence of occupied cells with 
\f0\b no gaps
\f1\b0  (consecutive integer coordinates, every cell between min and max occupied).\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 3. Definition of a Valid 
\f2\i Line
\f0\i0 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0
\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 A 
\f3\i line
\f1\i0  = exactly 2, 3, or 4 cards in a single contiguous segment (horizontal or vertical only; no diagonals).\
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 For a segment to be a valid line, 
\f0\b each
\f1\b0  of the three properties (color, shape, number) must be 
\f0\b either all identical OR all different
\f1\b0  across the cards in the segment.\
\pard\tx940\tx1440\pardeftab720\li1440\fi-1440\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl1\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Wild cards do 
\f0\b not
\f1\b0  have fixed properties; see \'a75 for assignment rules.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Any 2 cards automatically form a valid line (any two cards satisfy the condition for each property).\
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Maximum line length = 4 (impossible to have 5+ cards satisfying \'93all same or all different\'94 for any property with only 4 possible values).\
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Gaps destroy a line: any skipped coordinate means the cards on either side do 
\f0\b not
\f1\b0  form a line.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 4. Turn Structure & Actions\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0
\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Players: 2\'964. Hand size = exactly 4 cards at all times 
\f0\b except
\f1\b0  when draw pile is empty.\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Turn order: youngest player starts; play proceeds left (clockwise or counterclockwise \'97 app can choose).\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 On your turn you 
\f0\b must
\f1\b0  choose exactly one action:\
\pard\tx940\tx1440\pardeftab720\li1440\fi-1440\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl1
\f0\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Play action
\f1\b0 : Place 1\'964 cards from hand onto the grid following all GuideLines (\'a74.1). Then score (\'a77). Then replenish hand to 4 (draw from top of draw pile; if fewer than needed, draw all remaining).\
\ls4\ilvl1
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Pass action
\f1\b0 : Optionally trade 0\'964 cards from hand to the 
\f0\b bottom
\f1\b0  of the draw pile (player chooses order). Draw exactly as many new cards as traded to restore hand to 4.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 If draw pile is empty:\
\pard\tx940\tx1440\pardeftab720\li1440\fi-1440\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl1\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Play action: place cards \uc0\u8594  do 
\f0\b not
\f1\b0  replenish (hand size decreases).\
\ls4\ilvl1\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Pass action: still allowed (trade to bottom, but drawing 0 cards if pile empty).\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa319\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 4.1 GuideLines \'97 Legal Play Action (all must be satisfied)\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls5\ilvl0
\f1\b0 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 All cards played this turn 
\f0\b must lie in a single straight line
\f1\b0 :\
\pard\tx940\tx1440\pardeftab720\li1440\fi-1440\partightenfactor0
\ls5\ilvl1\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 All share the 
\f0\b same row
\f1\b0  (fixed y) 
\f0\b OR
\f1\b0  the 
\f0\b same column
\f1\b0  (fixed x).\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls5\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The played positions + all pre-existing cards in that same row/column 
\f0\b must form exactly one contiguous segment with no gaps
\f1\b0 .\
\ls5\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 At least 
\f0\b one
\f1\b0  played card must be orthogonally adjacent to at least one card already on the grid.\
\ls5\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	4	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 After placement, 
\f0\b every
\f1\b0  maximal contiguous segment (length 2\'964) on the 
\f0\b entire board
\f1\b0  that contains at least one newly placed card 
\f0\b must be a valid line
\f1\b0  (per \'a73).\
\ls5\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	5	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Cards may be placed in any order within the segment.\
\ls5\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	6	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 You may add cards to 
\f0\b both ends
\f1\b0  of an existing contiguous segment in the chosen row/column.\
\ls5\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	7	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Maximum cards per turn = 4.\
\ls5\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	8	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 You 
\f0\b cannot
\f1\b0  create gaps anywhere.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 5. Wild Card Rules (apply at all times)\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls6\ilvl0
\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 A Wild may substitute for 
\f0\b any
\f1\b0  possible card (even a duplicate of one already on the board).\
\ls6\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 When a Wild is placed (or already on board), it has 
\f0\b no fixed properties
\f1\b0  until needed for validation.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls6\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Consistency requirement
\f1\b0 : If a Wild is part of two or more lines, it must represent 
\f0\b the exact same
\f1\b0 (color, shape, number) in every line it participates in.\
\ls6\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Line validation with Wilds
\f1\b0 : A segment containing Wilds is valid 
\f0\b if and only if
\f1\b0  there exists at least one assignment of properties to each Wild in the affected lines such that:\
\pard\tx940\tx1440\pardeftab720\li1440\fi-1440\partightenfactor0
\ls6\ilvl1\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Every affected line satisfies the \'93all same or all different\'94 rule for each property.\
\ls6\ilvl1\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The assignment for each individual Wild is identical across all lines it belongs to.\
\ls6\ilvl1\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 (Brute-force feasible: at most 2 Wilds total, 64\'b3 = 262144 possibilities max per check.)\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls6\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Recycle action
\f1\b0  (optional, performed 
\f0\b before
\f1\b0  choosing your main action each turn):\
\pard\tx940\tx1440\pardeftab720\li1440\fi-1440\partightenfactor0
\ls6\ilvl1\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Select one Wild currently on the grid.\
